  - m_Id: 13057887209439232
    m_Localized: Discription
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 13057984500514816
    m_Localized: TYPES OF CHUNKS
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 13057949494853632
    m_Localized: "Sets how many individual \"chunks\" (segments) will appear consecutively
      in the level.\r"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 13058096987553792
    m_Localized: "There are five types of chunks:\r\n\r\n\u2022 Basic chunk \u2013
      a chunk with enemies and traps.\r\n\r\n\u2022 Ceiling chunk \u2013 a chunk
      with a ceiling and traps on it.\r\n\r\n\u2022 Grid platforms chunk \u2013 a
      chunk with platforms that the player jumps across.\r\n\r\n\u2022 Moving platforms
      chunk \u2013 a chunk with moving platforms that approach each other.\r\n\r\n\u2022
      Destructible chunk \u2013 a chunk with a collapsing floor."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 13058139958198272
    m_Localized: "Each chunk type has a weight value between 0.00 and 1.00 (the basic
      chunk has a minimum of 0.3). For each new chunk, the game takes the sum of
      all weight values and selects a chunk type proportionally to its share.\r\n\r\nFor
      example, if Basic = 0.8, Ceiling = 0.4, and others = 0.2 each, then the probabilities
      are:\r\n44% \u2013 Basic, 22% \u2013 Ceiling, 11% each \u2013 others.\r"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
